
##
# --- Connection Manager Options
#
# tp-connmgr is the connection chooser. It is the ThinStation equivalent of
# ThinPro's Connection Manager (the binary ThinPro confusingly calls
# hptc-kiosk) and, in a 'wm' session, it is the shell: there is no panel and
# no desktop, so this window is what the user sees.
#
# It is started from tp-wm-session when
# root/users/user/launchConnectionManager is 1. Set LAUNCH_CONNECTION_MANAGER
# in the tp-registry package's section to change that.
#
# Connections themselves live in the registry, not here. Manage them with the
# GUI, or from a shell with tpreg:
#
#   tpreg newconn freerdp "Office PC"
#   tpreg set root/ConnectionType/freerdp/connections/<uuid>/address srv.local
#
# --- Kiosk presentation
#
# root/users/<user>/kioskMode   When 1, the chooser is frameless, full screen
#                               and has no Add/Edit/Delete or Close. The user
#                               can pick a connection and nothing else.
#
#                               Note: ThinPro has a key at this same path but
#                               documents it as internal and reserved. Here it
#                               is a real, supported setting.
#
#   tpreg set root/users/user/kioskMode 1
#
# --- Who may edit connections
#
# root/users/<user>/switchAdmin When 0, Add/Edit/Delete are hidden even
#                               outside kiosk mode. Connections then come
#                               only from the shipped defaults or from a
#                               management system.
